{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Create a statutory right to receive offline & analogue customer services",
        "additional_details": "We feel the UK is becoming a mandatory digital society that removes the ability to live offline, and that basic tasks now penalise or exclude anyone without internet. Citizens face online-only workplace holiday bookings, fees for paper billing for utilities, and councils scrapping physical meters for app-only parking. Crucially, many GP surgery phone lines are gated by AI assistants who do not transfer to human receptionists. We believe a life without internet or AI should be a legally protected, penalty-free statutory right.",
        "background": "Create a statutory right to \u201cchoose offline services\u201d which mandates public bodies, utilities, banks and healthcare providers to provide accessible, penalty-free paper, phone and face-to-face contact, alongside digital and AI customer services.",
